From: FORZA-LAUNCHER-FOR-MAC-BLACKWELL-PROJECT
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Give each handle on a mapped image its own file position on macOS.

Applies on top of Ferestre's Wine series (icex/ferestre patches/wine 0001-0018,
in particular 0009 which introduced mapped_fd_to_handle()), checked against
xodus-gaming/wine bleeding-edge eab6973.

Ferestre 0009 serves NtCreateFile() on a WINE_DLL_FILE_MAP image from the
decrypted descriptor, and reopens that descriptor through /proc/self/fd so the
new handle gets an open file description -- and so a file position -- of its
own. macOS has no /proc: the open fails and the code falls back to the shared
descriptor. Every handle on the image then shares one position, with the loader
and with each other.

Forza Horizon 5 (Ferestre 0013) opens its own executable three times through
\\?\GLOBALROOT\??\Z:\..., hashes what it reads and stops the process when the
hash is wrong. With a shared position the first pass leaves it at end of file
and the second pass reads 0 bytes.

On macOS, reopen through the name fcntl(F_GETPATH) gives instead. That only
works while the file has a name; Xodus deletes it at once on macOS
(tempfile_in()), see patches/xodus-cli/0001 in this repository for the other
half. The reopened file must be the same device and inode as the descriptor.
When nothing works, the old fallback is kept and an ERR line says so once.

Tested: built in a Linux Wine tree (bleeding-edge + Ferestre 0001-0018 + this),
tools/mapfd_run.py + tools/selfread probe, see docs/ANALYSE-FH6-STORE-MACOS.md.
Not yet built or run on macOS.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
index a539cc5..0249c6e 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -1630,19 +1630,60 @@ static NTSTATUS open_mapped_dll_file( const UNICODE_STRING *nt_name, HANDLE *map
  * through /proc/self/fd gives a new open file description on the same object,
  * so each caller starts at zero.
  *
- * If /proc is not there, fall back to the descriptor itself rather than fail:
- * a shared offset is still better than no image at all, and that is what this
- * did before.
+ * macOS has no /proc. There the name F_GETPATH reports for the descriptor is
+ * opened instead, which gives a new open file description too -- but only
+ * while the file still has a name. Xodus on macOS writes the decrypted image
+ * to a temporary file on its RAM disk and deletes the name at once
+ * (tempfile_in()), so it has to keep the name for this to work; the Xodus half
+ * of this change does that.
+ *
+ * Either way the reopened file is checked to be the same object as the
+ * descriptor (device and inode): a name can be reused, and handing a title some
+ * other file under its own image's name would be worse than a shared offset.
+ *
+ * If no reopen works, fall back to the descriptor itself rather than fail: a
+ * shared offset is still better than no image at all, and that is what this
+ * did before. It is said once, because a title that hashes its own image three
+ * times then reads from the end of file on the second pass and stops itself,
+ * with nothing else in the log to say why.
  */
-static NTSTATUS mapped_fd_to_handle( int fd, HANDLE *handle )
+static int reopen_mapped_fd( int fd )
 {
+    struct stat st_fd, st_own;
+    int own_fd = -1;
+#ifdef F_GETPATH
+    char path[PATH_MAX];
+
+    if (fcntl( fd, F_GETPATH, path ) != -1) own_fd = open( path, O_RDONLY | O_CLOEXEC );
+#else
     char path[32];
+
+    snprintf( path, sizeof(path), "/proc/self/fd/%d", fd );
+    own_fd = open( path, O_RDONLY | O_CLOEXEC );
+#endif
+    if (own_fd == -1) return -1;
+    if (fstat( fd, &st_fd ) == -1 || fstat( own_fd, &st_own ) == -1 ||
+        st_fd.st_dev != st_own.st_dev || st_fd.st_ino != st_own.st_ino)
+    {
+        close( own_fd );
+        return -1;
+    }
+    return own_fd;
+}
+
+static NTSTATUS mapped_fd_to_handle( int fd, HANDLE *handle )
+{
+    static int warned;
     NTSTATUS status;
     int own_fd;
 
-    snprintf( path, sizeof(path), "/proc/self/fd/%d", fd );
-    if ((own_fd = open( path, O_RDONLY )) == -1)
+    if ((own_fd = reopen_mapped_fd( fd )) == -1)
+    {
+        if (!warned++)
+            ERR( "mapped image fd %d cannot be reopened (errno %d); every handle on it shares one "
+                 "file position\n", fd, errno );
         return wine_server_fd_to_handle( fd, GENERIC_READ | SYNCHRONIZE, 0, handle );
+    }
 
     status = wine_server_fd_to_handle( own_fd, GENERIC_READ | SYNCHRONIZE, 0, handle );
     close( own_fd );
